      "keyInsight": "We assume paying attention requires tightening our mental grip. But trying to force your mind still is like slapping choppy water to flatten waves. It only splashes more chaos across the surface. The breath is not an anchor you drop to lock down a ship. It is a steady rhythm you lean into. When you watch the breath without forcing it, you uncover a curious feedback loop. Your body sets the pace, and your mind settles down simply by observing the motion.",
